    "Specific ownership tax after the first year is not included because it is charged on the original sticker price.",
    "The registration base fee by weight is not included because the DMV page does not print it.",
    "The emissions area fee in the emissions program area, county road and bridge fees, and emissions testing are not included."
  ],
  "content": {
    "intro": "{state} charges {stateRate} state sales tax plus city, county and district tax where you live. Registration adds a specific ownership tax and a stack of smaller fees.",
    "howItWorks": [
      {
        "text": "Sales tax is figured on the purchase price less a trade-in, when the trade-in is itself a registered vehicle.",
        "sources": [
          "https://tax.colorado.gov/sites/default/files/documents/SUTT_Motor_Vehicles_November_2021.pdf"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Local taxes follow where you live and register the vehicle. A dealer collects a local tax only if you live in that place; otherwise you pay local use tax when you register.",
        "sources": [
          "https://tax.colorado.gov/sites/default/files/documents/SUTT_Motor_Vehicles_November_2021.pdf"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Specific ownership tax replaces property tax. It is a share of eighty-five percent of the original sticker price, and the share falls as the vehicle ages.",
        "sources": [
          "https://dmv.colorado.gov/taxes-and-fees"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Road and bridge safety surcharges depend on weight. An age-of-vehicle fee and several small fixed fees are added to every registration.",
        "sources": [
          "https://dmv.colorado.gov/taxes-and-fees"
        ]
      }
    ],
    "faq": [
      {
        "q": "Why does {state} registration cost so much in the first year?",
        "text": "Most of it is specific ownership tax, charged on the original sticker price at its highest rate in the first year. It drops each year after that.",
        "sources": [
          "https://dmv.colorado.gov/taxes-and-fees"
        ]
      },
      {
        "q": "Which local sales tax do I pay on a vehicle in {state}?",
        "text": "The tax for where you live and register the vehicle. A dealer in another town collects that town's tax only if you live there.",
        "sources": [
          "https://tax.colorado.gov/sites/default/files/documents/SUTT_Motor_Vehicles_November_2021.pdf"
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
}
